{"id":"chatcmpl-55fcbc67-3a09-47c1-8def-83dbd113d449","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244441,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task required distinguishing between left vs. right laterality of a basal opacity in a chest X-ray. The successful strategy combined an expert-model query for descriptive localization, a grounded findings report for coordinate verification, and phrase grounding to confirm that the candidate finding localizes to the correct anatomical region. The key insight is triangulating laterality across multiple independent evidence sources before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs. right), explicitly query for the anatomical side and location of the finding rather than the finding itself.\",\n    \"Use a grounded/coordinate-producing report to independently verify the spatial location suggested by a descriptive expert model.\",\n    \"Apply phrase grounding on the full candidate finding text to confirm it localizes to the expected anatomical region before selecting it.\",\n    \"Cross-check the same attribute (e.g., side) across at least two independent tools; agreement across sources justifies the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Radiology multiple-choice with laterality options\": \"Ask the expert model to describe location and appearance of the abnormality; then verify side with a coordinate-grounded report and phrase grounding.\",\n    \"Visual question answering with near-duplicate options\": \"Identify the single discriminating attribute between options (side, lobe, segment) and design queries that isolate that attribute.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence triangulation\": \"Sequence tools from descriptive (expert) to spatial (grounded report) to confirmatory (phrase grounding) to build converging evidence.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the discriminating attribute (e.g., left vs. right) is explicitly addressed by at least two independent tools.\",\n    \"Verify the final answer's phrase localizes to the correct anatomical region via grounding before submitting.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":517,"total_tokens":893,"completion_tokens":376,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":517},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":376}}}